  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Area Approximations: comparing trapezoidal and mid-ordinate estimates</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.2 (b, c, d) / Essential 2.1 (b, c, d): Find the trapezoidal and mid-ordinate estimates with 4 strips, compare them with a given exact area, and explain which is too big from the way the curve bends.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Exercise C, Question 5 in Chapter 9 of Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 3 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2005: the observation that one rule overestimates when the other underestimates, turned into a computed check against a given exact area; new polynomial curves.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
